  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The set of correct statements is:</p><p>(i)&nbsp;Manganese exhibits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math> oxidation state in its oxide.</p><p>(ii)&nbsp;Ruthenium and Osmium exhibit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math> oxidation in their oxides.</p><p>(iii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sc</mi></math> shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> oxidation state which is oxidizing in nature.</p><p>(iv)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> shows oxidising nature in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math> oxidation state.</p>"
  },
